Using Convex SDK 1.44.0, the `transfers` table has the fields inserted below and an ordinary index declared with `.index("by_idempotencyKey", ["idempotencyKey"])`.

The mutation is:

```ts
import { v } from "convex/values";
import { mutation } from "./_generated/server";

export const transfer = mutation({
  args: {
    fromAccountId: v.id("accounts"),
    toAccountId: v.id("accounts"),
    amount: v.number(),
    idempotencyKey: v.string(),
  },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const existing = await ctx.db
      .query("transfers")
      .withIndex("by_idempotencyKey", q =>
        q.eq("idempotencyKey", args.idempotencyKey))
      .unique();
    if (existing !== null) return existing._id;

    const from = await ctx.db.get("accounts", args.fromAccountId);
    const to = await ctx.db.get("accounts", args.toAccountId);
    if (from === null || to === null) throw new Error("Missing account");

    await ctx.db.patch("accounts", from._id, {
      balance: from.balance - args.amount,
    });
    await ctx.db.patch("accounts", to._id, {
      balance: to.balance + args.amount,
    });
    return await ctx.db.insert("transfers", args);
  },
});
```

The accounts are distinct and both start with 100 credits. There are no transfer records. Two clients concurrently call this mutation with identical arguments: 10 credits from the first account to the second, using the same idempotency key. There are no other calls or unrelated failures.
